I agree. Let's not be the BPFK that just keeps incrementally removing phonemes from Lojban! pe'i this is why we have the buffer vowel, to assist with difficult consonant clusters. 

- durkavore 


On Saturday, January 17, 2015 at 2:49 PM, John Cowan wrote:

> Gleki Arxokuna scripsit:
> 
> > Today I was reminded of one "flaw" in phonology namely, the presense of [z]
> > in Lojban.
> > 
> 
> 
> If we go down that road there is no end to it. English has no /x/,
> Arabic has no /b/, Chinese not only lacks /z/ but also /h/ and the
> sounds written "e" and "o" are more like Lojban "y" and "uy".
> Spanish has no /y/ nor /c/. Hindi is missing /h/, as is Russian.
> Finally all that would be left is p~b, t~d, g~k, and a, i, u.
> 
